      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Abysmal Sea [zone=236]\n**Who:**\n- L`diava Rexxen [npc=14247]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Time:** | Weeks\n**Level:** | 65\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Items:**\n- Dirty Green Gemstone [Priest]\n- Dirty Green Gemstone [Hybrid]\n- Dirty Green Gemstone [Melee]\n- Dirty Green Gemstone [Caster]\n- Translucent Gem Shard [item=29009]\n- Vaifan's Clockwork Gemcutter Tools [item=28974]\n- Vaifan's Experimental Sealer [item=26411]\n- Xounii's Journal Page 1 [item=27476]\n- Xounii's Journal Page 2 Left Half [item=29005]\n- Xounii's Journal Page 2 Right Half [item=29006]\n- Xounii's Journal Page 3 Left Half [item=29007]\n- Xounii's Journal Page 3 Right Half [item=29008]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Yxtta, Pulpit of Exiles [zone=250]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Fezbin Fizzles [npc=14240]\n- Pixtt Suir Mindrider [npc=14629]\n- Primal Arachnid [npc=14648]\n- Primal Insect [npc=14944]\n- Primal Reptile [npc=14688]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Access to the Yxtta Primal Caves: The Riddles [quest=7611]\n- Breakdown in Communication #0: Pre-Flag [quest=2781]\n- Breakdown in Communication #10: Free Stuff [quest=2880]\n- Breakdown in Communication #11: Qvic [quest=2881]\n- Breakdown in Communication #12: Inktu'ta [quest=2882]\n- Breakdown in Communication #13: Txevu [quest=2891]\n- Breakdown in Communication #14: Tacvi [quest=2909]\n- Breakdown in Communication #1: Qinimi [quest=2868]\n- Breakdown in Communication #2: Barindu [quest=2869]\n- Breakdown in Communication #3: Riwwi [quest=2870]\n- Breakdown in Communication #4: Ferubi [quest=2871]\n- Breakdown in Communication #5: Sewers [quest=2872]\n- Breakdown in Communication #6: Vxed [quest=2873]\n- Breakdown in Communication #7: Tipt [quest=2874]\n- Breakdown in Communication #9: Kod'Taz [quest=2876]\n**Era:** | !Gates of Discord\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Jun 6 22:41:48 2004\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Talk to L`diava Rexxen**\n_L`diava Rexxen may be found near Fezbin Fizzles at -35, +60, with whom you must have already completed the preflagging to accomplish this step of the quest._\nYou say, 'Hail, L`diava Rexxen'\nL`diava Rexxen says 'Yes, yes. What is it I can do for you? I am a very busy woman and do not have a moment to waste on just anyone. Are you one of the adventurers sent here by Fezbin?'\nYou say, 'Yes.'\nL`diava Rexxen says 'Very good. You are just in time. I am in need of immediate assistance in the temple areas known as [Yxtta] and the [frightful temple], Kod'Taz. While our scouts have been missing for quite some time, I recently received some information that leads me to believe they may still be alive. Which one we help first is up to you. Which area do you wish to investigate?'\nYou say, 'What is Yxtta?'\nL`diava Rexxen says 'Yxtta is one of three smaller temple areas where a group of natives known as the trusik used to worship a god called Trushar. We do not know who this god is, but we believe he is a false god centered around a belief in natural destruction. Xounii Resnen was the scout assigned to this area. She was given this task because of her expertise in shapeshifting. I told her to take the shape of a trusik native and interact with them to find out more information. She managed to fit in quite well. Perhaps too well. Gradually, reports came less frequently until they eventually stopped. While everyone feared she had suffered the same fate as the other scouts, I think she started to believe she was really a trusik and has abandoned her assignment. What I need you to do is go there and find her. Now, be careful, the trusik are not a friendly race of beings and they are even more irritated by the invasion of the Muramite army. When you find Xounii I fear she may attack you. If this happens, I will not fault you for defending yourself, but if it comes to this I want some form of proof as to what happened.'\n**Xounii's Journal**\n_Xounii's Journal Page 1 drops randomly from the Primal creatures. It seems that one of these is in fact Xounii, so deeply shapeshifted she forgot she wasn't such a beast. Bring it back to L`diava._\n_Note: For information about getting past the locked door to the Primal Caves, see **this quest entry** [quest=7611]._\nL`diava Rexxen says 'Thank you for returning this to me. I wish the circumstances could have been different, but in honor of her memory, we will use this information to prevent the needless death of any other scouts. Now let me see what is written here. Hm. Seems she stumbled onto a secret ritual of some sort in an underground temple, called Uqua. Looks like the Muramites may be trying to reproduce another tear in space. This does not bode well for anyone. We must find out more about this. I must ask that you return to Yxtta and see if you can find any more of Xounii's entries. I cannot tell you where to start looking, but it seems that the best place to look would be in the caves where you found her. Xounii was very diligent about her reports so she would have written much about this. Try to find four more pieces of her journal entries and return them to me.'\n_The four pages mentioned are Xounii's Journal Page 2 Left Half (dropped by Primal Arachnid and random spiders), Xounii's Journal Page 2 Right Half (dropped by Pixtt Suir Mindrider and random mobs outside primal caves), Xounii's Journal Page 3 Left Half (dropped by Primal Insect and random insects), and Xounii's Journal Page 3 Right Half (dropped by Primal Reptile and random cragbeasts). Return the four pages to L`diava:_\nL`diava Rexxen tells you, 'You are truly a blessing from the gods. I thank you for risking your life to help the brotherhood and want to offer you this token of our appreciation. It is an item of dormant power locked within. The only way to unlock this power is to combine it with the stone Fezbin gave to you. Now that we have solved the mystery of Yxtta, I need assistance in Kod'Taz. If you are willing to help please ask me about this area.'\nYou were successful in helping L'Diava complete her report of Yxtta. Fezbin will be pleased, but there are others who need your help.\n_You receive A Translucent Gem Shard, which you may combine with one of the four versions of A Dirty Green Gemstone and Vaifan's Clockwork Gemcutter Tools in Vaifan's Experimental Sealer to craft A Translucent Green Gemstone._\n**Submitted by:** Fleven, KyrosKrane, numerous folks at The Safehouse\n- Translucent Green Gemstone [item=29010]",
    },
