      walkthrough = "**Level:** 50\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nIs there a minimum faction/skill level/level required to get this text?\nFind Chef Chowderly at location -100, +175, +115, next to Tylida Eraldi, who shows up on /find.\nYou say, 'Hail, Chef Chowderly'\nChef Chowderly says 'Sorry, friend. I do not mean to be rude, but I am very busy right now cooking a [meal].'\nYou say, 'What meal?'\nChef Chowderly says 'I must cook for a large portion of the people living here on the ship. Seems they just cannot get enough of my cooking. I am a master at making [tasty tuna dishes] after all.'\nYou say, 'What tasty tuna dishes?'\nChef Chowderly says 'Are you interested in the culinary arts? If you are, then you must have heard of some of my most famous dishes such as my Seafarer's Tuna-Corn Chowder. You haven't heard of that you say? Hrmph. If you are interested in perhaps learning my award winning recipes, I could use a good assistant. Throgar over there is not much help!' Chef Chowderly gives a cold glance to his assistant Throgar who is standing in a small pile of broken dishes. 'I swear he drops more dishes than he cleans! Anyway, I might have time to teach you some recipes if you [can help] me with something and you have some knowledge of cooking.'\nYou say, 'I can help you.'\nChef Chowderly says 'First of all I need some more dishes.' Chef Chowderly glances over at Throgar again, who drops a glass on the ground, shattering it into tiny pieces. 'Sigh. I think I will need a lot of dishes. If you can, take this note to my friend Rellix in Rivervale. He owes me a favor and should be able to give you some dishes. Return them to me when you get them.'\nYou receive a Note to Rellix.  Rellix may be found in Rivervale near the /findable Byl Babbinsbort (location -135, -110, -8). Give him the note.\nRellix says 'A note from Chef Chowderly, eh? I haven't heard from him in some time. Hope he is doing well.' Rellix reads the note. 'I do happen to have some spare dishes. Here, take them.'\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a Case of Dishes.  Head back to Chef Chowderly and give him the case.\nChef Chowderly says 'Thanks much. These should last at least a day or so. Take this recipe for my world famous Spicy Tuna Salad Sandwich and see what you can do with it. Once you make one, hand it to me along with the recipe I just gave to you. Now, I don't let just anyone borrow recipes, so please pay attention and do your best.'\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a Recipe for Spicy Tuna Salad Sandwich, which reads:\nSpicy Tuna Salad Sandwich\nCombine in an Oven:\nOne 1 lb. Saltwater Tuna\nOne Loaf of Bread\nAlgae Spices\nKelp Garnish\nLettuce\nButter\n-Chef Chowderly\nMake one (trivial 202) and give it and its recipe scroll to Chef Chowderly.\nChef Chowderly scarfs down the dish you created. 'Nicely done! I can tell it was prepared with great care! Take this recipe for Pan-Seared Orange Tuna. It is a personal favorite of mine. Once you make this dish, hand it to me along with the recipe I just gave to you.' Chef Chowderly returns to his busy pace of cooking.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a Recipe for Pan-Seared Orange Tuna, which reads:\nPan-Seared Orange Tuna\nCombine in an Oven:\nOne 2 lb. Saltwater Tuna\nLoaf of Bread\nSpices\nSeaweed Vinegar\nFlask of Orange Juice\nCup of Sugar\nNon-Stick Frying Pan\n-Chef Chowderly\nMake one (trivial 215) and give it and its recipe scroll to Chef Chowderly.\nChef Chowderly scarfs down the dish you created. 'This is great. Your dish was flavorful, cooked just right, and I can tell you know your tuna. Take this recipe for Taelosian Tuna Kabobs. Once you make this dish, hand it to me along with the recipe I just gave to you.'  Chef Chowderly returns to his busy pace of cooking.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a Recipe for Taelosian Tuna Kabobs, which reads:\nTalosian [sic] Tuna Kabobs\nCombine in an Oven:\nOne 3 lb. Saltwater Tuna\nSkewers\nOne Spotted Mushroom\nOne Habanero Pepper\nGround Garlic\n-Chef Chowderly\nThe mushroom you need is \"A Spotted Mushroom,\" dropped in Dawnshroud Peaks.  Make one set of kabobs per the recipe (trivial 228) and give it and its recipe scroll to Chef Chowderly.\nChef Chowderly scarfs down the kabobs. 'Quality work! The tuna was cooked just right, the mushrooms were tender, and you added just enough peppers. I am impressed. Keep up the good work. Take this recipe for my Delightful Tuna Cakes. Once you make this dish, hand it to me along with the recipe I just gave to you.' Chef Chowderly returns to his busy pace of cooking.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a Recipe for Chowderly's Delightful Tuna Cakes, which reads:\nChowderly's Delightful Tuna Cakes\nCombine in an Oven:\nTwo 1 lb. Saltwater Tuna\nGround Garlic\nThree Shissar Eggs\nBread Crumbs\nOne Water Flask\nOne Cup of Flour\n-Chef Chowderly\nShissar Eggs drop from various shissar in Ssraezsha Temple.  Make one batch of cakes (trivial 242) and hand it and its recipe scroll to Chef Chowderly.\nChef Chowderly joyfully eats the cakes. 'This is great! You certainly know how to make this dish. Shissar Eggs are not easy to prepare properly, but you did an excellent job. We might have a master chef in the making here! I think these dishes have been too easy for you. From here on out, the recipes are going to be harder to make. I think you can handle it though. Take this recipe for Taelosian Tuna a la King. Once you make this dish, hand it to me along with the recipe I just gave to you.' Chef Chowderly returns to his busy pace of cooking.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a Recipe for Taelosian Tuna A La King, which reads:\nTalosian [sic] Tuna A La King\nCombine in an Oven\nOne 4 lb. Saltwater Tuna\nOne Bottle of Milk\nOne Cup of Flour\nOne Phoenix Egg\nOne Mushroom\nSpices\nVegetables\n-Chef Chowderly\nPhoenix Eggs drop in Doomfire, the Burning Lands and Eryslai, the Kingdom of Wind.  The mushroom is A Mushroom, which drops in Dawnshroud Peaks off the shrooms.  Make one batch of Taelosian Tuna A La King (trivial 268) and give it and its recipe scroll to Chef Chowderly.\nChef Chowderly joyfully eats the dish you prepared. 'This dish truly was fit for a king. Very nice work. Your training is almost complete. Take this recipe for Tuna Rice Surprise. Once you make this dish, hand it to me along with the recipe I just gave to you,' Chef Chowderly returns to his busy pace of cooking.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a Recipe for Tuna Rice Surprise, which reads:\nTuna Rice Suprise [sic]\nCombine in an Oven:\nOne 4 lb. Saltwater Tuna\nRice\nMature Cheese\nButter\nBread Crumbs\nJug of Sauces\nFish Oil\nWok\n`-Chef Chowderly\nMake one batch (trivial 282) and give it and its recipe scroll to Chef Chowderly.\nChef Chowderly joyfully eats your meal. 'Excellent work, my friend. I guess you want to know what the surprise part of the dish is? Well, there isn't one really. It is always nice to include the word surprise in at least one of your dishes! That is a tip you should never forget! Take this recipe for Spicy Tuna Sunrise Steak. Once you make this dish, hand it to me along with the recipe I just gave to you.' Chef Chowderly returns to his busy pace of cooking.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a Recipe for Spicy Tuna Sunrise Steak, which reads:\nSpicy Tuna Sunrise Steak\ncombine in an Oven:\nOne 4 lb. Saltwater Tuna\nVegetables\nOne Small Bottle of Soy Sauce\nGround Garlic\nOne Celestial Essence\nSpices\nOne Webbed Tail Fin\nNon-Stick Frying Pan\n`-Chef Chowderly\nWebbed Tail Fins drop in the Plane of Nightmare off of slarghilugs.  Make one batch (trivial 295) and give it and its recipe scroll to Chef Chowderly.\nChef Chowderly quickly engulfs your steak. 'Your dish was fiercely spicy and cooked just right. Very nice work. Your training is now complete. I present to you your rewards -- Chowderly's Grand Bowl and most importantly, a book containing all my great recipes! It has been a pleasure teaching you! I now send you forth into the world, hoping you feel confident with your tuna related cooking skills!'\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive Chowderly's Grand Bowl and Chef Chowderly's Tuna Recipe Compilation, containing all the recipes used in the quest.Submitted by: KyrosKraneRewards:\n- Chef Chowderly's Tuna Recipe Compilation [item=39152]\n- Chowderly's Grand Bowl [item=39149]\n[",
